---
/**
 * TEACHING & LEARNING · READING, LANGUAGE & LIBRARY — audit §2C.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND ITS TREATMENT IS UNTOUCHED — same
 * component, same photograph, same crop, same crumbs, same height, same title
 * and standfirst as before and as every other Academics page.
 *
 * ⚠ COMBINED PAGE — three of the brief's fourteen bullets: Reading Programme,
 * Language Development and Library Programme. In the school's own description
 * these are one effort seen from three sides.
 *
 * The page was rebuilt off the generic AcSplit → AcCollage → AcStatement →
 * AcPath → AcClose system into a composed one: five sections, five different
 * builds. Everything below the banner lives in
 * components/academics/teaching/ReadingLanguagePage.astro, and that file's
 * frontmatter carries the source for every claim — including the two places
 * this page departs from the design brief, and why.
 *
 * ⚠ SCOPE BOUNDARY — the library as a ROOM is inventoried on Laboratories &
 * Academic Clubs; here it is the collection and what is done with it.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import ReadingLanguagePage from '../../../components/academics/teaching/ReadingLanguagePage.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/photos/sb-library.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* ⚠ THE PANEL IS REQUIRED. PageHero is sticky and this panel covers it as the
      page scrolls; without it the banner hangs under the footer.

      ⚠ AND THE PADDING RESET IS AN INLINE STYLE, DELIBERATELY. `.u-page-panel`
      in base.css carries `padding-bottom: var(--sb-section-y)` — 120px of empty
      cream between the closing section and the footer. A stylesheet form of the
      override can be served from a different build than the HTML that needs it,
      and then it silently stops applying; an inline style travels IN the HTML,
      so the two cannot skew. Same decision as the other redesigned pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel" style="padding-block: 0;">
    <ReadingLanguagePage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
